# Scope of work

Read these rules before editing files, running git, or running the terminal.

- Do not commit, push, or open a pull request unless the user explicitly asks in the current message.
- Edit only the files the current task needs. Before changing a file outside that scope, ask and wait for confirmation.
- Do not run terminal commands on your own. Ask which command to run and wait for an explicit yes in the current message before running it.

Example: the task is to fix one widget. Do not also edit the workflow, unrelated tests, or commit those changes. If a test or `flutter` command would help, propose the exact command and wait. Run it only after the user says yes.
